    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2008-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\(\\dfrac{3}{5}=\\dfrac{M}{45}\\), we get \\(M=\\dfrac{3\\cdot45}{5}=27\\).\n\nFrom \\(\\dfrac{3}{5}=\\dfrac{60}{N}\\), we get \\(3N=300\\), so \\(N=100\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(M+N=27+100=127\\).\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Solve for \\(M\\) using \\(\\frac{M}{45}=\\frac{3}{5}\\).",
        "Solve for \\(N\\) using \\(\\frac{60}{N}=\\frac{3}{5}\\), then add."
      ],
